WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.350
- Have you ever wondered how much one

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:04.170
of these actually cost Apple to make?

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.490
Unfortunately, the company

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.290
doesn't release official profit margins

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.310
for its devices.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.380
That's why I reached out
to Counterpoint Research

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.030
for material cost breakdown.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.920
Some parts of the new phone are cheaper.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.590
But Apple kept the price we pay the same.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:17.490
Why is that?

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.560
Let's look at what the researchers found.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.410
- [Narrator] The best
iPhones we've ever created.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.470
- The iPhone 14 Pro Max
is the newest, priciest

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.290
and most feature-rich phone
you can get from Apple.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:29.580
It has the biggest display,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.780
a more advanced camera

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.970
and the fastest iPhone processor.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.820
So how much does all that
contribute to its cost?

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.050
Let's take a look at this chart.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:37.883
As you can see,

00:00:37.883 --> 00:00:39.600
the most expensive parts were the always

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.970
on display and the processing components.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:42.810
Together, they make up

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.730
about 40% of Apple's costs.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.220
The cellular parts cost about 13%.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.460
The cameras including the
new 48 megapixel main camera

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.990
only account for 11%.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:54.510
Other small parts like
the buttons, speakers

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.680
and internal controllers

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.300
make up the remaining costs.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.220
Overall, Counterpoint says Apple pays

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.340
about $464 for the parts of this phone.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.270
That's a tad bit more

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.390
than what Apple paid for
the iPhone 13 Pro Max.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.940
Despite the $17 rise in material costs,

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.950
Apple kept the retail price the same.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.140
Generally what it costs
to make an iPhone trends

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.190
upward over time.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.780
There are two big reasons for this.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.460
Number one is innovation.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.930
Premium phones keep getting better

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.910
and they have to to get your attention.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:21.990
Analysts suspect Apple

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.340
will continue raising prices

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.570
to offset innovation.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.510
- As you continue to see
more of that innovation

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:30.150
and giving the consumers
more of what they want

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.320
on that side of things,

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.120
pricing will continue to go higher.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.430
- [Dalvin] The original
iPhone reportedly cost Apple

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.620
about $218 to make.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:40.290
One of the biggest jumps
came a couple years back

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.060
between the basic iPhone 11

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.680
and the basic iPhone 12.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.690
Adding 5G to the iPhone 12,

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:48.360
switching from LCD to OLED screens

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.360
and other changes raised the cost 26%.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.750
The 5G components alone tacked on $34.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.120
But now 5G is the industry standard

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.040
and the reverse is starting to happen.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.660
The parts that enable cellular service

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.640
are cheaper than the previous generation.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.560
Number two, inflation.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.560
Adjusted for that, a
$649 iPhone 6 from 2014

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.420
would be about $896 today.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.010
But over time, you do start to get

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:14.910
more for your money.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.190
- A big strategy of Apple is actually

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.950
to use lower component prices

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.780
to pack more great content.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.400
So essentially pushing more

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.010
of the cost benefits to the consumer

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:26.970
through more content.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.250
- [Dalvin] These percentages
are just calculated estimates

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.270
because Apple's deals

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.890
with suppliers are top secret.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.900
While the iPhone maker
releases an annual list

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.490
of its suppliers, it doesn't say

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.560
how much business it
does with each company.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.840
Nor does it describe
what the suppliers do.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.210
One way Apple is dealing
with those rising costs

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.430
is by designing more parts in-house.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.500
Analysts say adding more homegrown parts

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.330
to devices should help bring costs

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.290
down over time.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.960
- If Apple wasn't getting
a cost benefit internally

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.310
designing their own chips,

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.170
they probably wouldn't be doing it.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.120
- Apple declined to
comment on this report.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.610
But the company does
control the vast majority

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.350
of smartphone industry profits.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.810
And pushing premium pro-level devices

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.562
helps it retain that lead.

00:03:05.562 --> 00:03:07.530
- (indistinct) Bigger benefit for Apple

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.540
than other hardware makers out there,

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:13.500
like PC vendors is Apple's brand allows it

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.660
to really sustain its elevated prices.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:16.830
- This strategy is important

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:19.140
to Apple's biggest
smartphone competitor, too.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.180
Samsung's high-end phones are also sold

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.250
for more than twice the cost of materials.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.410
The report doesn't tell
us how much Apple spends

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:26.610
on other critical parts

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.170
of its planning and distribution.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.700
We still don't know how much Apple spends

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.850
on sales and marketing,
shipping, or even retail

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.950
but the report does offer a decent glimpse

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.140
at what you're actually paying for.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.723
(upbeat music)

